During the 1974–75 Scottish football season, [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] competed in [[Scottish Division One]].

After winning the Scottish League an unprecedented nine times in a row, Celtic dropped to third place as they finished eleven points behind champions [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]].

Nevertheless, it was a successful season for the club as it won two major honours: the [[1974–75 Scottish Cup|Scottish Cup]] after defeating [[Airdrieonians F.C. (1878)|Airdrieonians]] 3-1 in the final, and the [[Scottish League Cup]] after they beat [[Hibernian F.C.|Hibernian]] 6-3.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/calgary-herald-glasgow-celtic-west-ham/158347853/|title=Glasgow Celtic, West Ham take soccer cups|work=[[Calgary Herald]]|date=3 May 1975|access-date=3 November 2024|page=3|via=[[Newspapers.com]]}}</ref>

Their European Cup campaign was cut short as they were eliminated in the first round by [[Greece|Greek]] champions [[Olympiacos F.C.|Olympiacos]], 1-3 on aggregate.

This was the final season as a player and captain for [[Billy McNeill]], who would later go on to manage Celtic in two separate spells between 1978 and 1991.

